stdout is deliberately unasserted: the dump enumerates every shipped playbook, skill and agent, and
the runner rejects on unequal line counts before any wildcard applies, so adding a core playbook
would break the case. What is pinned here is assembly — with no `.booping` marker on the cwd or any
parent, the vault-less branch of every loader still completes and the process exits clean. That
guards the class of loader regression that only shows up detached; it is not a contract on the
dump's content.

Twin of `an-attached-vault-assembles-without-error.txtar`, which covers the attached branch.

